# Laravel / PHP Rules

## Controllers

- Follow existing try/catch + `report($e)` pattern
- Auth checks: `Auth::user()->type == 1` for admin
- Use existing route naming in `routes/web.php`

## Models

- Models in `app/` with minimal Eloquent relations
- No new ORM packages

## Jobs & Events

- Queue jobs implement `ShouldQueue` like `GenerateSimulationHistoryReportJob`
- Broadcast events implement `ShouldBroadcast` like `PrivateMessageSent`

## Database

- Migrations in `database/migrations/`
- Also add SQL to `docker/mysql/` for existing Docker DBs
- MySQL 5.7 compatible only

## Example — simulation create side effect

When adding chat_users rows, update both `store()` and `update()` in `SimulationController.php`.
